---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout currentPath="/">
	<section class="hero-section">
		<h1 class="page-lead">
			Distributed systems and computational engineering.
		</h1>
		<p class="body-p">
			Podomy builds runtime infrastructure, simulation software, and systems engineering tools engineered from first principles for physical machines and decentralized networks.
		</p>
		<p class="body-p">
			All our core software is open-source under the AGPLv3 license. Commercial dual-licensing is available for organizations requiring proprietary integration and enterprise support.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">Projects</h2>
		</div>

		<div class="projects-mobile">
			<article class="project-card">
				<div class="project-card-top">
					<div>
						<a href="/concord/" class="project-title body-link">Concord</a>
						<p class="project-sub">Coordination</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="project-desc">
					Partition-native coordination layer for autonomous, offline-first machine workloads.
				</p>
				<div style="margin-top: 10px;">
					<a href="/concord/" class="body-link">Read specs &rarr;</a>
				</div>
			</article>
		</div>

		<table class="projects-table">
			<tbody>
				<tr>
					<td class="td-name">
						<a href="/concord/" class="body-link"><strong>Concord</strong></a>
					</td>
					<td class="td-role">
						Coordination
					</td>
					<td class="td-desc">
						<p style="margin: 0 0 8px;">
							Partition-native coordination layer for autonomous, offline-first machine workloads.
						</p>
						<a href="/concord/" class="body-link">Read specs &rarr;</a>
					</td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">Why this exists</h2>
		</div>
		<p class="body-p">
			Podomy exists to tackle the hardest problems in distributed systems, operating systems, and computational engineering. We build the software stack needed to run, coordinate, and simulate autonomous physical machinery without reliance on centralized infrastructure.
		</p>
		<p class="body-p">
			Our work spans partition-tolerant coordination protocols, low-level runtimes, geometric kernels, and simulation suites.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">Dual Licensing</h2>
		</div>
		<p class="body-p">
			We build in the open. Our core software is licensed under AGPLv3. For teams embedding Podomy technology into proprietary platforms without copyleft obligations, commercial licenses are available.
		</p>
		<p class="body-p">
			<a href="/licensing/" class="body-link">Learn more about licensing &rarr;</a>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<div class="section-header">
			<h2 class="section-title">Contact</h2>
		</div>
		<p class="body-p">
			We work directly with engineering teams building mission-critical software for physical and distributed systems. When you email us, you reach our core engineering team directly with a typical turnaround under 4 hours.
		</p>
		<p class="body-p">
			<a href="/contact/" class="body-link">Contact engineering &rarr;</a>
		</p>
	</section>
</Layout>
